"@@ -126,11 +126,11 @@ If you changed the store directory intentionally, run `pnpm install` and pnpm wi"," "," ## ERR_PNPM_UNSUPPORTED_ENGINE"," ","-A package's `engines.node` range does not accept the current Node.js version. The message names the package, the wanted range, and the current version.","+A project's `engines.node` or `engines.pnpm` range, or a dependency's `engines.node` range, does not accept the current version. The message names the package, the wanted range, and the current version."," ","-pnpm raises this error only with [`engineStrict`](./settings/cli.md#enginestrict) enabled. The check covers the project's own `engines` field and the `engines` field of every dependency. Without `engineStrict`, a dependency that does not accept the current version produces a warning.","+A project's incompatible `engines.pnpm` always raises this error. For `engines.node`, pnpm raises it only with [`engineStrict`](./settings/cli.md#enginestrict) enabled. Without it, an incompatible `engines.node` in the project produces a warning."," ","-To fix this error, switch to a Node.js version the package accepts, or turn `engineStrict` off.","+To fix this error, switch to a Node.js or pnpm version the package accepts, or turn `engineStrict` off for an `engines.node` mismatch."," "," ## ERR_PNPM_VIRTUAL_STORE_DIR_MAX_LENGTH_DIFF"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/docs/package_json.md","lines":["@@ -37,14 +37,13 @@ You can specify the version of Node and pnpm that your software works on:"," }"," ```"," ","-During local development, pnpm will always fail with an error message","-if its version does not match the one specified in the `engines` field.","+If the project's `engines.pnpm` does not accept the running pnpm version,","+the install fails."," ","-Unless the user has set the `engineStrict` config flag (see [settings]), this","-field is advisory only and will only produce warnings when your package is","-installed as a dependency.","-","-[